    &lt;div class="banner-content"&gt;
      &lt;h2 class="banner-title"&gt;Billing Notice&lt;/h2&gt;
      &lt;p class="banner-message"&gt;
        We detected the following message: 
        &amp;lt;script&amp;gt;alert('billing');&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;
      &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/section&gt;

Implementation notes:
- The user-supplied content appears escaped as text inside the paragraph, using &amp;lt; and &amp;gt; for angle brackets.
- Avoid setting innerHTML with untrusted data; use textContent/innerText or server-side escaping when interpolating into templates.
- ARIA attributes (role="status", aria-live="polite") help screen readers announce non-intrusive status updates.
- No inline event handlers or script tags are present.

If you share your exact banner classes or structure, I can adapt this sample to match your DOM and CSS more closely.

